  "id": "Compound::DB00177 - Disease::DOID:9352",
  "verbalization": "Valsartan, a member of the angiotensin II receptor antagonists, is linked to Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus through its pharmacological properties and molecular similarities with other drugs in the class. The evidence suggests that Valsartan, through its structural resemblance to Tasosartan and Forasartan, shares a common pathway with Losartan, which is known to treat Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus. This relationship is further supported by the shared ancestry with Losartan, which itself is part of a broader class of drugs that influence vascular function and metabolic regulation. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which Valsartan may exert its effects on glucose metabolism, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence points to a dependency on angiotensin II receptor antagonism as a key pathway, but the precise role of this mechanism in diabetes treatment requires further investigation.",
